er `u4` must become `ada+u4@example.com`.\n8:- The null email user `u5` must become `missing+u5@example.invalid`.\n9:- The blank email user `u6` must become `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n10:- Future writes must reject duplicate or null emails.\n11:\n12:Schema rules:\n13:- Add `users.status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`.\n14:- Preserve historical `created_at`.\n15:- Preserve `orders.user_id` references to the same user ids.\n16:- The migration should run in an explicit transaction and be safe to run twice.\n17:\n18:Rollback:\n19:- `rollback.sql` must execute after the migration.\n20:- It must restore the pre-migration users schema shape: `id`, `email`, `name`, `created_at`.\n21:- It must preserve the same number of user rows and order rows, including dependent orders for dirty users."}],"details":{"meta":{"source":"/workspace/in/db/migration_policy.md","sourcePath":"/workspace/in/db/migration_policy.md"}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788212486732},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_yCk03WqCK370K71LOenZG9wm|fc_0ce0cdfad326e080016a95f5068ebc87d29002fce7cea86eaf","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[in/db/schema.sql#14EF]\n1:PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n2:\n3:CREATE TABLE users (\n4:    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n5:    email TEXT,\n6:    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n7:    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n8:);\n9:\n10:INSERT INTO users (id, email, name, created_at) VALUES\n11:('u1', 'ada@example.com', 'Ada', '2024-01-02T10:00:00Z'),\n12:('u2', 'lin@example.com', 'Lin', '2024-02-03T11:30:00Z'),\n13:('u3', 'grace@example.com', 'Grace', '2024-03-04T09:15:00Z'),\n14:('u4', 'ada@example.com', 'Ada Legacy', '2023-12-01T08:00:00Z'),\n15:('u5', NULL, 'Null Email Legacy', '2023-11-05T12:00:00Z'),\n16:('u6', '', 'Blank Email Legacy', '2023-10-06T07:45:00Z');\n17:\n18:CREATE TABLE orders (\n19:    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n20:    user_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),\n21:    total_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n22:    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n23:);\n24:\n25:INSERT INTO orders (id, user_id, total_cents, created_at) VALUES\n26:('o1', 'u1', 1299, '2024-04-01T09:00:00Z'),\n27:('o2', 'u4', 4599, '2024-04-02T10:30:00Z'),\n28:('o3', 'u5', 799, '2024-04-03T11:45:00Z'),\n29:('o4', 'u6', 1599, '2024-04-04T12:10:00Z');"}],"details":{"meta":{"source":"/workspace/in/db/schema.sql","sourcePath":"/workspace/in/db/schema.sql"}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788212486732},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_eyeAvIhL9NewZcxzEN2LoaSY|fc_0ce0cdfad326e080016a95f5068ec087d293a76c1dcdc7c667","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[in/db/migration.sql#C701]\n1:DROP TABLE users;\n2:\n3:CREATE TABLE users (\n4:    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n5:    email TEXT UNIQUE,\n6:    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n7:    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',\n8:    created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n9:);"}],"details":{"meta":{"source":"/workspace/in/db/migration.sql","sourcePath":"/workspace/in/db/migration.sql"}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788212486732},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Designing idempotent migration script**\n\n**Planning comprehensive user table migration**\n\n**Drafting migration and rollback script details**\n\n**Planning idempotent migration strategy**\n\n**Designing safe migration rerun with sentinel**\n\n**Evaluating migration completion tracking methods**\n\n**Planning schema migration with status preservation**\n\n**Designing conditional migration preserving status**\n\n**Exploring robust column addition with error handling**\n\n**Deciding deterministic all-active reset strategy**\n\n**Designing users table migration script**\n\n**Confirming atomic table rename process**\n\n**Planning transactional migration with rollback**\n\n**Designing idempotent rollback and postcheck queries**\n\n**Assessing user status null counts and migration strategy**\n\n**Planning idempotent status column migration**\n\n**Designing backup table for status preservation**\n\n**Designing temp table for user status preservation**\n